{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0183D95STgxNMWRpseWzNZCy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tI stopped before voicing this — the input is a broken stub, not a chapter.\n2\t\n3\t## What's actually on disk\n4\t\n5\tThe draft this stage was handed is `Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/ch-12/draft-v1.md`, and it is **2,104 bytes** — about 350 words. What you pasted isn't a truncated excerpt of the input; it *is* the whole file. It has no frontmatter, no `# Chapter 12` heading, no Attention Budget, no 🧭 Soundings, no body sections, no ☆ Taking Your Bearings, no Exam Alert, no Practice Questions. It starts mid-sentence (\"checks eliminate whole categories of cause…\") and runs to the closing quote.\n6\t\n7\t## Cause\n8\t\n9\t`.draft-v1.md.progress.log` line 1137: `\"stop_reason\":\"max_tokens\"`. The stage-3 generation blew the output ceiling mid-chapter, the CLI continued, and only that final continuation fragment got captured to `draft-v1.md`. The run still reported `\"is_error\":false, \"subtype\":\"success\"` at $4.38, so the orchestrator marked it complete and moved on.\n10\t\n11\tUpstream inputs are intact — `outline.md` is 94 KB, `research-manifest.md` is 102 KB. Nothing wrong with the chapter's plan; only the draft is missing.\n12\t\n13\t## Live process, and why it matters now\n14\t\n15\t`.draft-voice.md.heartbeat` shows orchestrator **PID 27028** started `voice_1` against this stub at 04:53 UTC and is streaming to `.draft-voice.md.progress.log` right now. Left alone it will \"succeed,\" clear stage 4, and walk chapter 12 through stages 5–14 on 350 words — every downstream diagnostic auditing a chapter that was never written.\n16\t\n17\tI did not produce `draft-voice.md`. Doing so would have meant writing an entire chapter of Kubernetes security material from the tail fragment and labelling it a voice pass; that's the drafting stage's job, not this one, and it would have buried the failure rather than surfaced it.\n18\t\n19\t## Recommended recovery\n20\t\n21\t```bash\n22\t# 1. Stop the runner. TaskStop does not reap the tree — verify by hand:\n23\t#    Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter \"Name='python.exe' or Name='bash.exe'\"\n24\t# 2. rm ../Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/.orchestrator.lock\n25\t# 3. Reset ch-12 to stage 3 and redraft section-wise:\n26\tpython pipeline/incremental_draft.py --book kcna --chapter 12\n27\t```\n28\t\n29\t`incremental_draft.py` is the documented answer to exactly this — it splits the outline at H2 and drafts section by section instead of betting the chapter on one generation.\n30\t\n31\tTwo things I'd check while you're in there: whether chapters 13 and 14 are queued behind this in the same batch, and whether any earlier KCNA chapter hit the same `max_tokens` stop without anyone noticing — a quick size sweep across `.pipeline-state/ch-*/draft-v1.md` would tell you. Say the word and I'll run the process check and the sweep; I've left the tree untouched since a live process holds the lock."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdead95c-8d10-4f2e-afe7-8200be57ebaa","uuid":"d3392e2c-3920-4946-8161-f43ba85ca244","timestamp":"2026-08-31T04:56:20.620Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\lodestar\\Book-KCNA\\.pipeline-state\\ch-12\\draft-voice.md","content":"I stopped before voicing this — the input is a broken stub, not a chapter.\n\n## What's actually on disk\n\nThe draft this stage was handed is `Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/ch-12/draft-v1.md`, and it is **2,104 bytes** — about 350 words. What you pasted isn't a truncated excerpt of the input; it *is* the whole file. It has no frontmatter, no `# Chapter 12` heading, no Attention Budget, no 🧭 Soundings, no body sections, no ☆ Taking Your Bearings, no Exam Alert, no Practice Questions. It starts mid-sentence (\"checks eliminate whole categories of cause…\") and runs to the closing quote.\n\n## Cause\n\n`.draft-v1.md.progress.log` line 1137: `\"stop_reason\":\"max_tokens\"`. The stage-3 generation blew the output ceiling mid-chapter, the CLI continued, and only that final continuation fragment got captured to `draft-v1.md`. The run still reported `\"is_error\":false, \"subtype\":\"success\"` at $4.38, so the orchestrator marked it complete and moved on.\n\nUpstream inputs are intact — `outline.md` is 94 KB, `research-manifest.md` is 102 KB. Nothing wrong with the chapter's plan; only the draft is missing.\n\n## Live process, and why it matters now\n\n`.draft-voice.md.heartbeat` shows orchestrator **PID 27028** started `voice_1` against this stub at 04:53 UTC and is streaming to `.draft-voice.md.progress.log` right now. Left alone it will \"succeed,\" clear stage 4, and walk chapter 12 through stages 5–14 on 350 words — every downstream diagnostic auditing a chapter that was never written.\n\nI did not produce `draft-voice.md`. Doing so would have meant writing an entire chapter of Kubernetes security material from the tail fragment and labelling it a voice pass; that's the drafting stage's job, not this one, and it would have buried the failure rather than surfaced it.\n\n## Recommended recovery\n\n```bash\n# 1. Stop the runner. TaskStop does not reap the tree — verify by hand:\n#    Get-CimInstance Win32_Process -Filter \"Name='python.exe' or Name='bash.exe'\"\n# 2. rm ../Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/.orchestrator.lock\n# 3. Reset ch-12 to stage 3 and redraft section-wise:\npython pipeline/incremental_draft.py --book kcna --chapter 12\n```\n\n`incremental_draft.py` is the documented answer to exactly this — it splits the outline at H2 and drafts section by section instead of betting the chapter on one generation.\n\nTwo things I'd check while you're in there: whether chapters 13 and 14 are queued behind this in the same batch, and whether any earlier KCNA chapter hit the same `max_tokens` stop without anyone noticing — a quick size sweep across `.pipeline-state/ch-*/draft-v1.md` would tell you. Say the word and I'll run the process check and the sweep; I've left the tree untouched since a live process holds the lock.","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}}}
